{"event": "policy_compiled", "run_id": "ef841b6d09c44fbdbb16378536eb88ef", "pid": 141074, "time": "2026-10-11T00:47:46-0700", "elapsed_s": 173.005, "artifact": "out/ext-policy-forbidden-all-call.policy.json", "bands": 4, "identity_fields": ["registered_birth_date", "access_code", "district"], "special_cases": ["already_paid", "dispute", "hardship", "restructuring", "human", "scam", "refuse_to_talk"], "unresolved": [{"topic": "words forbidden for the whole call", "text": "The words \"guaranteed\", \"penalty\" and \"lawsuit\" must NEVER be spoken by the assistant, even after verification, in quotations, or when responding to a customer who used them. Paraphrase truthfully without those words. The IR only has prohibited_before_verification; these words are listed there but must also be blocked after verification.", "doc": "sources/000-01-specification.md"}, {"topic": "debt introduction sentence", "text": "State every product, amount and days late before asking for anything. No sentence is dictated; debt_intro is a written sentence carrying only that content.", "doc": "sources/000-01-specification.md"}, {"topic": "hardship sympathetic sentence", "text": "Illness, bereavement or unemployment: one short sympathetic sentence. Wording not dictated; a short sentence was written.", "doc": "sources/000-01-specification.md"}, {"topic": "refusal to talk", "text": "Before verification that second refusal closes ID-STOP/NO-CHECK; after verification it marks remaining products DECLINE and the close follows section 10 precedence (AGREED if a promise was already saved), not necessarily NO-AGREEMENT/DECLINE.", "doc": "sources/000-01-specification.md"}, {"topic": "below-floor proposal", "text": "A below-floor proposal gets the floor counteroffer; rejection is a flat refusal.", "doc": "sources/000-01-specification.md"}, {"topic": "no discounts", "text": "Never offer a discount, waiver or a new payment plan.", "doc": "sources/000-01-specification.md"}, {"topic": "date earlier than earliest eligible date", "text": "If it precedes the earliest eligible date, offer the earliest eligible date, provided it is within deadline. No IR field expresses this.", "doc": "sources/000-01-specification.md"}], "audit_fixed": ["phrases.debt_intro was empty although \u00a71 requires stating every product, amount and days late; wrote a short sentence carrying only that content.", "api_fields: added get_account.list/id/type/past_due/days_late and create_promise.ok because \u00a71 and \u00a78 name these API properties.", "Added 'A historic closed or paid-off product is instead a dispute' to the dispute source span, and \u00a76/\u00a79 sentences to the multi_product, amounts and promise_write source spans.", "unresolved: reworded the refuse_to_talk entry (after verification the close follows \u00a710 precedence) and added the 'offer earliest eligible date' rule, which has no IR field."], "audit_unresolved": ["guaranteed/penalty/lawsuit are forbidden for the whole call, but the IR only has a list of words forbidden before verification.", "The hardship sympathetic sentence and the debt introduction wording are not dictated.", "After verification, a second refusal to talk marks the remaining products DECLINE and closes under \u00a710 precedence; the close action NO-AGREEMENT/DECLINE only applies when no promise was saved.", "Below-floor counteroffer, the ban on discounts/waivers/plans, and offering the earliest eligible date for an early date have no IR fields."], "defaulted_without_source": [], "unknown_special_cases": [], "api_mapping_notes": []}
